1
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:03,906
Between the sixth and seventh books there's

2
00:00:03,926 --> 00:00:06,956
a short story called Strange Dogs.

3
00:00:06,976 --> 00:00:08,781
It takes us to Laconia,

4
00:00:08,801 --> 00:00:11,106
the hidden world where Winston Duarte

5
00:00:11,126 --> 00:00:12,856
and his rogue Martians went after

6
00:00:12,876 --> 00:00:14,156
the Ring battle.

7
00:00:14,176 --> 00:00:14,981
It's the bridge

8
00:00:15,001 --> 00:00:16,781
to the final three books,

9
00:00:16,801 --> 00:00:17,556
and to a jump

10
00:00:17,576 --> 00:00:19,681
of nearly thirty years.

11
00:00:19,701 --> 00:00:21,069
Spoilers ahead!

12
00:00:21,776 --> 00:00:22,906
Cara is a young girl

13
00:00:22,926 --> 00:00:24,731
whose family came to Laconia

14
00:00:24,751 --> 00:00:26,706
with the Martian settlers.

15
00:00:26,726 --> 00:00:27,931
Near her home,

16
00:00:27,951 --> 00:00:30,006
she finds strange creatures that look

17
00:00:30,026 --> 00:00:31,606
a little like dogs.

18
00:00:31,626 --> 00:00:33,306
They are not animals.

19
00:00:33,326 --> 00:00:35,566
They are alien repair machines,

20
00:00:35,586 --> 00:00:38,301
left behind by whoever built the gates,

21
00:00:38,321 --> 00:00:41,081
and they can fix almost anything that's broken.

22
00:00:41,782 --> 00:00:43,662
Then her little brother Xan is killed

23
00:00:43,682 --> 00:00:45,012
in an accident.

24
00:00:45,032 --> 00:00:46,612
Cara takes him to the dogs,

25
00:00:46,632 --> 00:00:48,487
and they bring him back to life.

26
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:50,862
But Xan is not quite the same.

27
00:00:50,882 --> 00:00:52,412
His body has been rebuilt

28
00:00:52,432 --> 00:00:54,562
by alien technology.

29
00:00:54,582 --> 00:00:58,807
Duarte's scientists, led by Paolo Cortazar,

30
00:00:58,827 --> 00:01:00,382
one of the scientists behind

31
00:01:00,402 --> 00:01:01,992
the Eros disaster,

32
00:01:02,012 --> 00:01:03,632
take a close interest.

33
00:01:04,337 --> 00:01:06,092
Cortazar has a short story

34
00:01:06,112 --> 00:01:06,862
of his own,

35
00:01:06,882 --> 00:01:08,787
called The Vital Abyss.

36
00:01:08,807 --> 00:01:10,262
After Eros, he

37
00:01:10,282 --> 00:01:12,687
and the other Protogen scientists are locked

38
00:01:12,707 --> 00:01:13,662
in a cell,

39
00:01:13,682 --> 00:01:16,012
prisoners of a group of Martians.

40
00:01:16,032 --> 00:01:18,112
Looking back, he feels no guilt about

41
00:01:18,132 --> 00:01:19,712
the people of Eros.

42
00:01:19,732 --> 00:01:22,862
He only wanted to understand the protomolecule.

43
00:01:22,882 --> 00:01:24,887
So when Duarte offers him the chance

44
00:01:24,907 --> 00:01:26,262
to keep working on it,

45
00:01:26,282 --> 00:01:27,262
he takes it,

46
00:01:27,282 --> 00:01:29,316
and follows him to Laconia.

47
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:32,362
That is the lesson of Laconia.

48
00:01:32,382 --> 00:01:34,997
The gate builders left their tools behind,

49
00:01:35,017 --> 00:01:37,372
and Duarte means to use them.

50
00:01:37,392 --> 00:01:38,997
Ancient alien platforms

51
00:01:39,017 --> 00:01:41,747
in orbit build him warships unlike anything

52
00:01:41,767 --> 00:01:43,717
humanity has made.

53
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:45,742
For nearly thirty years he waits

54
00:01:45,762 --> 00:01:48,277
and builds, and makes himself the ruler

55
00:01:48,297 --> 00:01:49,656
of a new empire.

56
00:01:50,365 --> 00:01:53,595
Back home, those thirty years pass in peace.

57
00:01:53,615 --> 00:01:56,045
The Transport Union runs the gates,

58
00:01:56,065 --> 00:01:58,395
the Rocinante crew grows older,

59
00:01:58,415 --> 00:02:01,440
and Holden starts to think about retiring.

60
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,620
Then the gate to Laconia opens,

61
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,620
and a warship like nothing anyone

62
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,470
has seen comes through.

63
00:02:07,490 --> 00:02:10,926
Next up: book seven, Persepolis Rising.

